          (0, true), (1, true), (2, true), (6, true), (0, true), (1, true), (2, true), (6, true),
          (0, true), (1, true), (2, true), (6, true)]] := by
  simp only [GroupPresentation.relatorLetters_def, GroupPresentation.relators_def,
    suzPresentation_transcribed, List.map_cons, List.map_nil, Relator.toWord_mul,
    Relator.toWord_pow, Relator.toWord_inv, Relator.toWord_gen, FreeGroup.invRev]
  decide

/-- The lengths of the thirty-four compiled relator words of `Suz`, in the order of the
transcription: the seven involution relations, the twenty-one pair relations, and then the six
words appended after the Coxeter paths.

Reading the counts off one relator at a time is what lets a reviewer locate a discrepancy, rather
than only observe one in the total of `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_totalLength`. -/
theorem suzPresentation_map_length_relators :
    suzPresentation.relators.map List.length =
      [2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 10, 6, 16, 6, 6, 8, 6,
        4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4,
        9, 5, 20, 15, 78, 20] := by
  rw [← GroupPresentation.map_length_relatorLetters, suzPresentation_relatorLetters]
  decide

/-- The compiled relators of the `Suz` presentation contain `275` signed letters in total. This is
read off from the spelled-out letters rather than from the record. The source publishes no
presentation length, so the figure states the transcribed data for a reviewer to compare against
the source and is not matched to a published number. -/
theorem suzPresentation_totalLength : suzPresentation.totalLength = 275 := by
  rw [← GroupPresentation.sum_map_length_relatorLetters, suzPresentation_relatorLetters]
  decide

/-- Every compiled relator of the `Suz` presentation is cyclically reduced. This is what would make
the letter count of `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_totalLength` comparable with a published
presentation length, which is measured after free and cyclic reduction of each relator. Every
compiled word here being already cyclically reduced, that length is the `275` of
`TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_totalLength` itself. -/
theorem suzPresentation_relatorsCyclicallyReduced :
    suzPresentation.relatorsCyclicallyReduced := by
  -- Only the relator compiler needs unfolding: once the transcribed expressions are compiled away,
  -- the words are closed data and the kernel decides the predicate.
  simp only [GroupPresentation.relatorsCyclicallyReduced_iff, GroupPresentation.relators_def,
    suzPresentation_transcribed, List.map_cons, List.map_nil, Relator.toWord_mul,
    Relator.toWord_pow, Relator.toWord_inv, Relator.toWord_gen, FreeGroup.invRev]
  decide

end TauCeti.Sporadic
